- mesa_wire

' This mount is the switch that gives a world its foot at /<self>/io/mesa. All
' of the foot is in src/foil. When a world starts with this mount, the mount
' calls mesa_wire/start, and that function registers the foot.
'
' The foot gets no information from outside the world:
' - The first time, the foot makes its seed.
' - The foot keeps its two files where its record says, or in io/mesa/.
' - If its record holds a port, the foot listens on that port.
'
' A port and the cards of peers are ordinary records. Any door or a hand can
' write them.
+ mesa_mount
  + start
    \ server=nat self=iota arguments=row[str]
    ^ nat
    | mesa_wire/start server self arguments
